on class="gd-task" id="discount-games-and-leads-leads" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Leads</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renter leads</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles: plays, claims, codes on booking requests, bookings, revenue and discounts from game codes in the last 30 days, then the same by game and by prize (Play again shows its plays; it has no claims).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each claim: when, the name (and &quot;on the site now&quot;), email and phone, the prize and game, the code and whether it is used (with the booking), marketing consent, and the visit: cars and pages viewed, minutes, city and device. A person who won again shows &quot;2nd code of 2&quot; under the name on each of their lines.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Contacted</b> (it is yours). <b class="gd-ui">Close</b> with a reason when there is nothing more to do. A booking with the code marks the lead converted by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A visitor who viewed 3 cars or more also gets a Sales task, for example &quot;Claimed 10% off, viewed 6 cars: Maya&quot;. It closes when the code goes on a request. A new code while that task is open is added to it, not a second task.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="discount-games-and-leads-contact-details-typed-into-forms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Contact details typed into forms</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renter leads</b>, the card &quot;Typed into forms&quot; at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When someone types a name, email or phone into the request to book, the contact form, List your car, the owner application, Create an account, the discount game or the chat, it is saved as soon as each field is valid, even if they never press Send.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line: when, the name (and &quot;On the site now&quot;), email and phone, the form, and Sent or Not sent. &quot;Email not confirmed&quot; means the account was opened from the form and the person has not opened the link we emailed them yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">After 30 minutes without sending, To do shows &quot;Unfinished request from Maya Chen: follow up&quot; (not raised from 23:00 to 07:00, the quiet hours of the site alerts). Call or email them; the task closes by itself when they send the form.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Only what they typed is saved, and never used for offers without their consent.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A new email gets an account at once (no password, email not confirmed) and one email &quot;Continue your request&quot; 30 minutes later, between 9:00 and 21:00. Until they open its link they cannot accept an offer, sign, pay or upload documents. An account never confirmed closes after 30 days; the lead stays. It is on by default; the times and the To do are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, the card &quot;Forms left unfinished&quot;.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="discount-games-and-leads-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settings</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Discount games</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>On or off, the cap for percentage codes ($75), how long a code is good for (7 days), when it shows (2nd page view, 30 seconds, exit intent), the days a visitor keeps their prize (14: closing never draws a new one, and a prize not claimed pops up again until then), the days after a claim before the game comes back (1; 0 is one code per person ever), how often Play again works on a prize not claimed (once a day; 0 turns it off), and the cars viewed for a Sales task (3). The reminders before a code ends are under Promo codes.</li><li>At most one game a visit by default (a setting), and a visit ends after 30 minutes away (a setting): the next page brings the game again. With more than one a visit, the next card shows on their 3rd page view after a close (any page) or 2 minutes later, whichever first; no daily cap unless you set one. A prize waiting for them pops up once a visit only. All are settings. Never on booking, payment or signing pages; the request-to-book form has its own game.</li><li>Prizes and games: each prize with its percent, dollars or free days, a minimum rental length, its cap and its chance, or Play again (another go, at most one); each game&#39;s weight (0 turns it off). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save prizes and games</b>. Codes already sent keep their value.</li></ul></section>');
-- GUIDES 0351 END
